        // highest triangle hit on a 0.5 mm grid in the pocket's nose-intersection
        // frame, one ray per bearing from the fitted outer centre, one lateral
        // line per leg station, the model's OWN band edges on each ray, medians
        // per 15° bin ±7° / per 10 mm leg span, std ≤ 0.3 on every row used).
        // `rows` are the section's t rows above the wall top that the reads
        // hang on: crest (0.151), shoulder (0.41), plateau (0.6 / 0.855), wall
        // top (1.0), plus a 0.03 witness 1.4 mm clear of the inner face; the
        // two inner-face rows (t 0 / 0.004) ride with that witness by the
        // section's own offsets at the apex (DERIVED). Bearings are degrees from
        // the outboard axis; leg spans are mm in front of the tangent row.
        // The 0° row IS the recorded section where it has a row (the read
        // gives 55.9 / 45.8 / 43.0 / 42.4 on the corner, 56.0 / 45.6 / 43.0 /
        // 42.4 on the side); 0.03 and 0.6 are read verbatim.
        // What it changes: the model's plateau and wall top RISE toward the
        // tangent rows and along the legs (corner wall top 42.3 → 43.8 at 90°
