      // INSIDE the cushion back so the wood|cloth boundary carries no
      // daylight. That tuck is a second boundary 2 mm from the real one, and
      // the section census reads it for what it is — the rail solid and the
      // cushion solid interpenetrating down every rail (measured: 2.00 mm,
      // 6 cushions x 2 crossings each, plus a 283 mm FAIL arc where the side
      // pocket's cut-out closes inside the bay). The boundary law wants ONE
      // shared curve, so the Predator takes 0: the rail's inner face IS the
      // cushion back plane, the two faces are coincident and mutually hidden
      // below the cushion top, and the seam sections as a TOUCH. No daylight
      // is possible between coincident planes.
      railLap: 0,
