// ---- GH-621 (catalog v18): the Diamond Pro-Am SIZE VARIANTS ---------------
// The 8 ft and 7 ft Pro-Am are the SAME furniture on a smaller bed, and the
// official factory drawings say so in their own arithmetic: rail band
// (overall − play)/2 = 7.0 in on both axes of all three sizes, leg inset
// (overall − legs)/2 = 7 1/8 in on all three, rail-top height 32 in and
// floor clearance 15 in on all three (dossier-diamond-proam/01-official/
// official-specsheet-{7,8,9}ft-proam.png; docs/geometry/diamond-proam-
// {8,7}ft-table-definition.json, DERIVED from the 9 ft sheet by
// tools/render/gh488d/derive_size_variant_621.py). So the render entry is a
// DERIVATION, not a copy: the kernel mirror is the 9 ft mirror with only
// length/width replaced — exactly what the kernel does (PocketTableSpec::
// diamond_proam_{8,7}ft = diamond_proam_9ft by struct update), so the boot
// drift gate compares identical numbers per id — and the render block is
// shared by reference, because every render key is a per-size-invariant
// furniture fact (frameWidth = the 7.0 in band − CW, bedAboveFloor = 32 in −
// the 2 in stack, legStanceIn = 7 1/8 in, skirtFloorClear = 15 in, the
// pocket collar, the K55 section). The two things that DO scale with the bed
// — sight positions (addSights: L/8, W/4) and pocket placement — are
// computed from G.L / G.W downstream, never stored here. Sharing the
// reference also states the honest limit in code: the 8/7 ft entries carry
// no look of their own; anything wrong with the 9 ft furniture is wrong on
// them too, and anything fixed on the 9 ft is fixed on them.
//
// Pocket furniture invariance is corroborated, not drawn: the official
// drawings carry NO pocket dimension (JSON open item O7). What the drawings
// DO dimension per size lands here as length/width only.
export function diamondProAmSize(base, { length, width }) {
  return {
    kernel: { ...base.kernel, length, width },
    render: { ...base.render, gully: null }, // GULLY-FIX1: the side-panel openings + sleeves follow a per-size export; only the 9 ft has one
  };
}
