// coverage floor with ~2x-thick cords at the old pitch — same scalar,
// wrong character ("broad flat straps forming a bright basket"; the R1
// fall read 0.62-0.73 white vs the paired photos' own 0.43-0.49).  The
// lattice moves to the references' FINE-cord construction: 9 cells per
// tile (12.9 mm surface / ~6.8 mm projected at the R2 boot plane — the
// TPT/Joy/q8pro cord class) at the gate-prescribed width 0.38-0.52 of
// the (now smaller) cell, more knots (one crown per crossing, 9x9),
// and — density law — the reference's 0.76-0.82 body coverage comes
// from thin cords CLOSE TOGETHER, so the width RATIO stays ~0.5 while
// the absolute cord width drops ~2.3x.  On the solid-ground lower bag
// a half-pitch-offset DIM UNDERLAYER (0.70L) draws first: the bunched
// bag's own deeper cord layers (the q8pro body is layered cotton, not
// black holes), which also carries the references' deep white V range
// (their white p05-p95 spread 47-49 vs rev-14's 24-25).  The r13
// aperiodicity fix is KEPT (phase-periodic wander, params keyed
// (family, k mod 9), integer wobble cycles over the overshoot span);
// the round-14 four-pass cylindrical cross-section + radial knot
// crowns are KEPT at the finer width (cord-roundness law).
