  // measured 0.82 vs the black-PRC factory band 0.90-1.30 — the specular
  // loss is repaid in albedo, keeping T1 in band from every angle).
  // GH-488D wave A2 (ATTEMPTED AND REVERTED — envMapIntensity stays DEAD
  // here on purpose; do not re-wire it without re-running the live gate).
  // The 'wood' mode above bought the casting the box-projected env, but NOT
  // a level: envMapIntensity is a dead knob for scene.environment-lit
  // materials unless a spikeEnvGain holder is wired, and the measured
  // consequence is that the env leg supplies 82 % of the casting's whole
  // rendered value (probe row w_env_off: p85 V 0.259 -> 0.047 at the
  // r1_corner_macro register). Wiring the holder therefore looks like the
  // lever for the OWNER-LAW casting/rail-top ratio, and the isolated probe
  // agreed — masked p85 V at r1_corner_macro:
  //     gain   casting p85   rail p85   ratio
  //     0.00      0.047        0.071     0.66   <- authored / shipped
  //     0.25      0.110        0.106     1.04
  //     1.00      0.259        0.208     1.25   (as-built)
  // Factory law from the #484 photo synthesis: 0.90-1.30 on black PRC,
  // 0.57-0.72 on rosewood/golden-oak; the e2e-lighting T1 gate wants
  // castingLum/railLum in [0.55, 1.45]. The probe's 1.04 did NOT survive
  // contact with the gate. The env cube is baked at the room-box centre and
  // CONTAINS THE TABLE, so raising the rail's and casting's own gain also
  // raises what they contribute back into the bake; at the gate's own owner
  // pose the rail gained more than the casting and T1 went the wrong way:
  //   authored (this file)  T1 0.722  (casting 44.4, rail 61.5)  PASS
  //   gain 0.25 everywhere  T1 0.548  (casting 25.5, rail 46.5)  FAIL
  // i.e. the probe's single-register p85 and the gate's whole-frame mean
