      woodMat.clearcoat = 0.15; woodMat.clearcoatRoughness = 0.6; // RC-24 clearcoat / clearcoat_roughness — review round 9 P2: at 0.4 / 0.5 the rig's room map still read as a champagne brushed grain — the cap must stay black under the register lights // RB-06 high-gloss cap (HLD t0140 reflection); A2 build 6: coat roughness 0.10 → 0.25, base 0.28 → 0.40 — the rig's linear light strips mirrored as brushed-metal streaks along the cap
      woodMat.envMapIntensity = 0.03; // RC-24: RETAINED at the r9 value and DISCLOSED as inert — the knob is dead for scene.environment-lit materials (roxEnvCube header) and the cap has always been lit by the scene cubemap. It is left in place because that cubemap IS the room: a black gloss cap beside blue cloth really does carry the bounce (measured b -0.3 lit / +4.0 shaded), and an own cube takes the cap to luma 0 (probe D/E, corner_3q)
