      // The mouth's existing casting and short interior liner retain the
      // fall dressing. No second opaque bag or floating bottom disc is
      // placed inside the visible, supported outer net.
      // GH-490 round-5 (audit r3 N4) HISTORY: a flush BAY PLATE
      // (cn8-bayplate-*, beamMat) used to stand behind each side
      // pocket's skirt drape — the long-rail planks stop against the
      // bulge (cn8LeftRailPlanHalves) and the plate filled the cut band
      // FLUSH with the flanking plank faces, the Q8 Pro side
      // reference's dark frame face below the pinked hem.
      // r12-APPROVED (card 17b): the middle throat casting (cn8-mid-throat /
      // cn8-mid-liner), its cove clip and the 62° cloth cone cn8-cloth-midfall
      // RETIRE with the plate contract — the slate cut face is lined by the
      // cloth band FL-02 and the pocket's back wall is the leather body's own
