        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // CRAFT-UPLIFT R1 item 3 — support loops on the nose wrap
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // MEASURED DEFECT (not assumed).  Per-vertex normal turn across this
        // band's columns, all 49 chords, both jaws of corner 5:
        //   col 0->1  med 52.8  max 56.5    <-- the fold
        //   col 1->2  med 10.2  max 16.0
        //   col 2->3  med  3.7  max 38.2
        //   col 3->4  med 18.9  max 25.1
        // Column 0 IS the nose-roll apex line and its normal is forced to +Y
        // (an apex normal is +Y by definition); the very next station is
        // 1.8-3.0 mm away up a 42-59 deg facet.  The roll is therefore
        // resolved by ONE facet and lands as a hard fold — a folded dart.
        // Where the wrap is resolvable it reads as a flat lit slab that ends
        // in a hard cut against the under-rail shadow, with no turning
