        // apex condition the builder already asserts) and m1 = the outgoing
        // facet slope — the classic support-loop result, and the unique cubic
        // meeting both conditions.  Its off-coordinate is unchanged, so no
        // station moves in plan; its z stays inside [z(col0), z(col1)]
        // because dz/du = dz*(6u-6u^2) + off1*m1*(3u^2-2u) is positive over
        // (0,1) for every chord on this part.  The nose apex (col 0, z =
        // H_NOSE) and every original station are byte-identical: this only
        // ADDS interior loops.
        //
        // WHAT THE PART ACTUALLY IS.  On the deep profile the outgoing run
        // is a PLATEAU (profDep stations 1 and 2 share z = 0.039), so
        // m1 = 0 and the joint is a riser between two horizontal runs, not a
        // roll into a slope.  Every C1 curve across such a riser must peak
        // ABOVE the chord slope; the cubic's 1.5x is the minimum available
        // (a sinusoidal ease peaks at pi/2 x).  So the cure here cannot
        // flatten the roll — it can only remove the two curvature
        // discontinuities that bracketed it.
        //
        // LOOP PLACEMENT — measured, after a uniform-spacing attempt FAILED.
        // First cut used u = q/(n+1) with n = 4.  Re-measuring the same turn
        // table on the built mesh:
        //   col 0->1  med 51.69  max 59.76   <-- the fold, UNMOVED
        //   col 1->2  med 11.96   col 2->3  med  1.41
        //   col 3->4  med  5.24   col 4->5  med 16.60  max 42.49
        // i.e. uniform loops smoothed the roll's middle and left both ENDS
        // exactly as folded as before.  That is predictable and was the
        // error: for a smoothstep |z''| = |6 - 12u| * dz is MAXIMAL at u = 0
        // and u = 1 and ZERO at mid-span, so uniform spacing puts loops
        // where there is no curvature to resolve.  Chebyshev-Lobatto
        // spacing, u_q = (1 - cos(pi*q/(n+1)))/2, clusters them at both ends
        // — where the curvature is.
        //
